  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Follow the Money: An Effective Roadmap for Freedom of Expression</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">* Monitor, document and denounce violations of freedom of expression
* Monitor the socio-economic rights of journalists
* Conduct audience research and social media sentiment analysis on attitudes towards freedom of expression in Lebanon
* Track statements of political actors on freedom of expression matters
* Investigate the Lebanese media sectors&#x2019; funding and ownership
* Investigate international foreign aid (US, UK, EU, Canada, France, and the Netherlands) to the Lebanese Army, security institutions and judiciary sector, and assess the aid&#x2019;s intended and unintended impact on freedom of expression
*Large-scale communication and engagement about the findings of all research components</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To improve rule of law, human rights, and freedom of expression standards in Lebanon.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022;	Journalists, media professionals (including photojournalists, cameramen/women and media technicians), and news providers. 
&#x2022;	Media outlets 
&#x2022;	Social media users 
&#x2022;	Democracy activists and HRDs 
&#x2022;	Marginalized communities (refugees, migrant workers, LGBTIQ+ etc.)
&#x2022;	The Lebanese public at large</narrative>
  </description>
